aether-joc

src/tables_gen.rs (generated by tools/gen_tables.py) and tools/ts_103420_tables.c
contain the JOC Huffman code tables (annex A.1) and the QMF prototype filter
QWIN (clause 7.4, called prot64 in the source file). They are normative data of
ETSI TS 103 420 V1.2.1 (2018-10), taken from ts_103420v010201p0.zip which
accompanies the specification (https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/103400_103499/103420/01.02.01_60/).
(C) ETSI 2018, (C) European Broadcasting Union 2018. The tables are included
because an implementation cannot interoperate without them; the rest of the
crate is written from the text of ETSI TS 103 420 and ETSI TS 102 366 annex H.

The C# project Cavern (github.com/VoidXH/Cavern) was deliberately NOT read:
its licence forbids selling the code and requires the author's permission for
public use, which is not compatible with this project.

The crate depends (path, read-only) on aether-ac3 (LGPL-2.1-or-later).
